  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "As-cast equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr has 8–16% room-temperature tensile ductility.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "As-cast equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr has a yield strength of 163–530 MPa at 1000 °C.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "As-cast equiatomic HfNbTaTiZr has a characteristic solid-solution microstructure.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding approximately 3–5 at.% Al to HfNbTaTiZr will significantly improve its oxygen resistance.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "An Al addition of approximately 3–5 at.% will not degrade the alloy's intrinsic high-temperature strength and ductility.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Homogenization after casting will ensure uniform distribution of the added Al.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "During high-temperature exposure, Al will segregate to the surface of the modified alloy.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Surface segregation of Al will produce a continuous, adherent Al2O3 scale.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed Al2O3 scale will act as an oxygen-diffusion barrier.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al2O3 barrier will reduce oxygen ingress and oxidation of the underlying HfNbTaTiZr-based alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Reduced oxygen ingress will preserve the alloy's microstructure and inherent high-temperature mechanical properties.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "After approximately 100 hours at 1000 °C in air or a controlled oxygen atmosphere, the Al-modified alloy will have lower oxidation weight gain than untreated cast HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "After the oxidation exposure, the Al-modified alloy will have better oxide-scale integrity than untreated cast HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al-modified alloy will retain high-temperature yield strength similar to that of untreated cast HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Al-modified alloy will retain tensile ductility similar to that of untreated cast HfNbTaTiZr.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Keeping Al at approximately 3–5 at.% will avoid detrimental phase changes or brittle intermetallic formation.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Casting followed by homogenization will maintain the beneficial mechanical properties of the original alloy.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
